text:
They use this framework: <a href="https:&#x2F;&#x2F;learnbchs.org" rel="nofollow">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;learnbchs.org</a><p>Their example is:<p><pre><code>    #include &lt;err.h&gt; &#x2F;* err(3) *&#x2F;
    #include &lt;stdlib.h&gt; &#x2F;* EXIT_xxxx *&#x2F;
    #include &lt;stdio.h&gt; &#x2F;* puts(3) *&#x2F;
    #include &lt;unistd.h&gt; &#x2F;* pledge(2) *&#x2F; 
    int main(void)
    {
      if (pledge(&quot;stdio&quot;, NULL) == -1) 
        err(EXIT_FAILURE, &quot;pledge&quot;);
        puts(&quot;Status: 200 OK\r&quot;);
        puts(&quot;Content-Type: text&#x2F;html\r&quot;);
        puts(&quot;\r&quot;);
        puts(&quot;Hello, world!\n&quot;);
        return EXIT_SUCCESS;
      }</code></pre>
